<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_ScarlandsGraveWardScatter.xml   UtinniPatches - SCARLANDS_MECHANICS_2 build pass continuation

  Places RUT_SentinelGraveWard on the map and closes the "OWED, NOT BUILT:
  faction assignment" gap that ThingDef's own header flagged — see
  RUT_GenStep_ScatterSentinelGraveWards.cs (src/RimMandrake/EnvironmentalHazards/
  Source/) for the full mechanism note. Without this GenStepDef the grave-ward
  was never placed on any real map at all: the building def existed, and
  RUT_LordJob_SentinelDefend/RUT_SentinelDefend existed, but nothing ever
  spawned the building, so the whole §4 Sentinel mechanic was dead content.

  order 960: just after RUT_ScarlandsSprungDangers' own 955 (dressing scatter)
  and ScarlandsJunkPrefabs' donor 950 — a grave-ward is a real building
  (needs a clear, standable, unoccupied cell, same CanPlaceAt gate
  GenStep_ScatterSacredWalls uses), so it runs after the dressing/junk
  scatters that could otherwise claim its cell first.

  A plain GenStepDef, not a Patch: campaign-mechanic content wired directly
  onto the frozen RUT_Scarlands twin, same precedent RUT_ScarlandsSprungDangers
  already set in this same folder. Not wired into RM_Warscar
  (SCARLANDS_STANDALONE_MOD_1's franchise-free mod) — that mod's own header
  states this class of content stays UtinniPatches-only.

  Wired into RUT_Scarlands.xml's own extraGenSteps by this pass — see that
  file's own header for the added <li>.
-->
<Defs>

  <GenStepDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_ScarlandsGraveWardScatter</defName>
    <order>960</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RUT_GenStep_ScatterSentinelGraveWards">
      <thingDef>RUT_SentinelGraveWard</thingDef>
      <chancePerMap>0.15</chancePerMap>
      <countRange>1~1</countRange>
      <minEdgeDistance>8</minEdgeDistance>
    </genStep>
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
